      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[3,8],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=3$ and $b=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(8-3)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{25}{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{12}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{6}≈1.443.\n$$",
